    title: "Iron Age – Assyria, the Phoenicians and archaic Greece",
    hegemon: "<strong>Assyria</strong> is the first military superpower: siege technology, a standing army, mass deportations as a tool of rule. Its brutality proves its undoing – in 612 BC half the known world allies to destroy Nineveh. Babylon, the Medes, Lydia and Egypt then briefly share power until Persia swallows them all.",
    text: "<p>Iron replaces bronze – weapons and tools become cheap and widely available, distributing power more broadly. The Phoenicians invent the <b>alphabet</b> and settle the Mediterranean (Carthage, 814 BC); the Greeks adopt it and found hundreds of colonies from Spain to the Black Sea.</p><p>In Israel/Judah monotheism sparks a religious revolution; the Babylonian exile (587 BC) shapes Judaism to this day.</p>",
