    kunst: "<p>Greek vase painting develops from geometric to figurative style; the first stone temples appear, forerunners of the later Doric order. In Assyria, monumental palace reliefs with winged bull colossi (lamassu) flank the gates of Nineveh and Nimrud – war propaganda in stone, often with dramatic lion-hunt scenes.</p>",
