    text: "<p>Hellenism is the first “globalization”: Greek becomes the world language, Alexandria with its library the world's centre of science (Euclid, Archimedes, Eratosthenes – who calculates the Earth's circumference!).</p><p>Rome, a farmers' republic with a unique system of alliances, wears Carthage down – Hannibal's crossing of the Alps (218 BC) is in vain. But conquest tears the Republic apart from within: landless veterans, overmighty generals (Marius, Sulla, Caesar, Pompey) and civil wars end with Caesar's dictatorship, his assassination (44 BC) and the victory of his heir Octavian.</p>",
