    text: "<p>Augustus transforms the shattered Republic into a stable empire – the <b>Pax Romana</b>. Cities flourish from Britain to Syria: 80,000 km of roads, aqueducts, law (“Roman law” echoes in modern codes to this day). Under Trajan (AD 117) the empire reaches its greatest extent.</p><p>In Judaea, Christianity grows out of the preaching of Jesus of Nazareth – at first a persecuted fringe sect, within 300 years the imperial religion. Meanwhile Han China invents paper and introduces civil-service examinations – rule by the educated instead of the hereditary nobility.</p>",
