    text: "<p>Europe awakens: the population doubles, forests are cleared, towns founded, the first universities appear (Bologna 1088, Paris, Oxford). In 1066 the Normans conquer England (Battle of Hastings). In 1054 Christendom splits into Catholic and Orthodox.</p><p>In 1095 Pope Urban II calls the crusade: in 1099 the crusaders take Jerusalem (with a terrible massacre). For almost 200 years crusader states and Muslim rulers fight – in 1187 Saladin retakes Jerusalem. A side effect of the crusades: trade and knowledge from the Orient galvanize Europe.</p>",
