    text: "<p>The 90s begin hopefully: waves of democratization, European unification (EU 1993, euro 2002), the internet for everyone, the end of apartheid in South Africa (Mandela 1994). But also: the Yugoslav wars with the genocide of Srebrenica (1995), and the genocide in Rwanda (1994 – ~800,000 dead in 100 days).</p><p>11 September 2001 marks the turn: the “war on terror”; the Afghanistan and Iraq wars tie down the USA for two decades. The financial crisis of 2008 shakes confidence in Western capitalism. The smartphone (2007) and social media revolutionize communication – with light and shadow. Climate change becomes the recognized question of humanity (Kyoto 1997, Paris 2015).</p>",
